\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Light of light, enlighten me,
\par Now anew the day is dawning,
\par Sun of grace, the shadows flee,
\par Brighten Thou my Sabbath morning;
\par With Thy joyous sunshine blest,
\par Happy is my day of rest!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Fount of all our joy and peace,
\par To Thy living waters lead me;
\par Thou from earth my soul release,
\par And with grace and mercy feed me;
\par Bless Thy word that it may prove
\par Rich in fruits that Thou dost love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Kindle Thou the sacrifice
\par That upon my lips is lying;
\par Clear the shadows from mine eyes;
\par That, from every error flying,
\par No strange fire may in me glow
\par Which Thine altar doth not know.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Let me with my heart to-day,
\par Holy, holy, holy, singing,
\par Rapt awhile from earth away,
\par All my soul to Thee upspringing,
\par Have a foretaste inly given
\par How they worship Thee in heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Rest in me and I in Thee,
\par Build a paradise within me;
\par O reveal Thyself to me;
\par Blessed Love, who diedst to win me;
\par Fed from Thine exhaustless burn,
\par Pure and bright my lamp shall burn.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Hence all care and vanity,
\par For the day to God is holy;
\par Come, Thou glorious Majesty,
\par Deign to fill this temple lowly;
\par Nought to- day my soul shall move
\par Simply resting in Thy love.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

